learnings:
  - The ReDoS was invisible to code review and tests at small sizes — only timing a doubling series exposed the quadratic curve; always time n, 2n, 4n on detector regexes.
  - Leak probes caught two real leaks the builders didn't anticipate (/find echoing q; link text naming a hidden note) — sentinel-based probes over every output surface are worth their cost.
  - 'A loopback guard is not an origin boundary: any local dev server is ''localhost''. Exact origin + HttpOnly cookie is the minimum for a personal-data UI.'
  - Tamper hashes introduce their own races with legitimate writers; write pending-hash first and re-check before pausing.
  - BIP39 seed-phrase detection skipped (no vetted wordlist in repo) — follow-up.
